From 76c9a926ad01a51cd1d9e9b805fef68af7e7f55e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:03:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): a restart-lost queue card whose message already
 ran stops painting the chat red on every route [daveey]

An unknown card (a turn the owner lost in a restart) paints its chat red until the
owner's next pending snapshot drops it or the user discards it. Only a provably local
route gets that snapshot in the background, so on a hub route a card whose message ran
again kept the chat red after everything finished, while the backend's own status said
nothing was wrong (self-heal desktop-d94ca254ae).

On each session-list refresh, a red chat whose row shows no live turn now reads its
stored transcript passively (REST, never session.resume): a user row newer than the card
carrying its submission id or its words (merged turns included), answered by an
assistant reply before the next user turn starts (rows stored as _queued_prompt ride
the running turn), settles the card. The reply is required, since the lost run itself
stored its user row. The journal entry is dropped rather than retired, so a later
snapshot that still lists the card unknown repaints it with its Discard.

The red stripe's tooltip now names this cause: A message queued before a restart may
not have run: Send again or Discard.
